  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(\\sin A=\\frac{2}{3},\\) \\(\\cos A=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{4}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt5}{3}.\\) Because \\(B=90^\\circ-A,\\) we have \\(\\tan B=\\cot A\\) and \\(\\frac{\\cos A}{\\sin A}=\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Angles \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are complementary",
        "Use \\(\\cos A=\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2A}\\) and \\(\\tan B=\\cot A\\)"
      ],
